description: Real-Time Streaming and Events rules for FinShield AI
globs: backend/app/streaming/**, frontend/src/hooks/use-socket.ts, backend/app/api/v1/webhooks.py
---

Streaming Stack:
- Azure Event Hubs (Kafka-compatible)
- Socket.IO (python-socketio on backend, socket.io-client on frontend)
- Webhooks

Streaming & Event rules:
- High-throughput transaction ingestion must be handled via Azure Event Hubs.
- Stream processors must handle partitions and maintain offsets reliably.
- Use Dead Letter Queues (DLQ) for failed event processing after 3 retries.
- WebSockets are strictly for pushing real-time updates (alerts, live transactions, metrics) to the frontend.
- Emit specific events to namespaces (e.g., `/alerts`, `/transactions`, `/dashboard`).

Webhook expectations:
- Webhooks must support HMAC signature verification for security.
- Implement exponential backoff for webhook delivery retries (max 5 retries).

Do not:
- Block the main event loop while waiting for Event Hub messages.
- Use WebSockets for standard CRUD operations (use REST API instead).
- Send sensitive PII over WebSockets without encryption or masking.